    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 0,
        "text": "10 May 1940. Army Group B invades the Netherlands and Belgium. The British and French rush north into Belgium to meet it, as the Germans hoped."
      },
      {
        "t": 1.5,
        "text": "Meanwhile seven panzer divisions wind through the hills and forests of the Ardennes, thought too difficult for tanks."
      },
      {
        "t": 3,
        "text": "13 May: under heavy dive-bombing, German infantry cross the Meuse at Sedan. The French armies there begin to collapse."
      },
      {
        "t": 5,
        "text": "15 May: the Netherlands surrender, a day after Rotterdam is bombed. The panzers race west across open country towards the sea."
      },
      {
        "t": 10,
        "text": "20 May: German tanks reach the Channel near Abbeville. The best Allied armies are cut off in the north."
      },
      {
        "t": 14,
        "text": "24 May: Hitler halts the panzers outside Dunkirk for three days, to rest them and let the Luftwaffe finish the job."
      },
      {
        "t": 16,
        "text": "26 May – 4 June: Operation Dynamo. Warships and hundreds of small boats lift about 338,000 soldiers off the beaches and harbour of Dunkirk."
      },
      {
        "t": 19,
        "text": "Belgium surrenders on 28 May. The rearguard holds the perimeter while the evacuation goes on; nearly all the heavy equipment is left behind."
      },
      {
        "t": 25,
        "text": "4 June: Dunkirk falls. Less than three weeks later France signs an armistice."
      }
    ]
  },
