    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 0,
        "text": "19 November 1942. Germany's Sixth Army is fighting for the ruins of Stalingrad. Its long flanks on the Don and the open steppe are held by weaker Romanian armies."
      },
      {
        "t": 1,
        "text": "Operation Uranus: Soviet armies smash through the Romanian 3rd Army north-west of the city. Next day a second blow falls in the south."
      },
      {
        "t": 4,
        "text": "23 November: the two pincers meet near Kalach. About a quarter of a million Axis soldiers are trapped."
      },
      {
        "t": 6,
        "text": "Hitler forbids a breakout. Göring promises to supply the pocket by air."
      },
      {
        "t": 12,
        "text": "The airlift delivers a fraction of what is needed. Men begin to starve in the frozen steppe."
      },
      {
        "t": 23,
        "text": "12 December: Manstein's relief force attacks from the south-west."
      },
      {
        "t": 30,
        "text": "It gets within about 50 km of the pocket. Paulus does not break out to meet it."
      },
      {
        "t": 35,
        "text": "A new Soviet offensive on the Don threatens to cut off the relief force too. It falls back."
      },
      {
        "t": 45,
        "text": "January: the Soviets demand surrender and are refused. The pocket is crushed piece by piece and the last airfields are lost."
      },
      {
        "t": 73,
        "text": "31 January 1943: Paulus, promoted to field marshal the day before, surrenders."
      },
      {
        "t": 75,
        "text": "2 February: the last troops in the northern pocket surrender. About 91,000 prisoners march into captivity."
      }
    ]
  },
